{"id": 14, "ts": 1780480149.5761478, "event": "public_discussion_message", "round": 1, "agent": "emily_brooks", "message": "I\u2019m inclined to align with Sarah\u2019s provisional recommendation of Candidate\u202fC. The 100\u202f% reliability record and the consistently positive crew atmosphere directly address two of our most critical criteria\u2014operational reliability and crew cooperation. Moreover, C\u2019s ability to make correct decisions quickly speaks to decision quality under pressure, which is essential for long\u2011distance flights.\nThat said, we still need to weigh the strong points of the other candidates before finalising. Candidate\u202fB is very conscientious, handles stress very well, and excels at assessing weather conditions and computer\u2011based tasks\u2014clear assets for technical competence and stress resilience. However, the notes that B is regarded as pretentious and sometimes adopts the wrong tone raise serious concerns about professional communication and crew cooperation.\nCandidate\u202fD shows excellent problem\u2011solving, concentration, and a serious sense of responsibility, all valuable for technical and cognitive competence. Yet the observations that D is moody and considered a loner could undermine crew cooperation and professional communication.\nGiven that C\u2019s proven reliability and crew rapport outweigh the unknowns for A and the mixed signals for B and D, I would provisionally recommend Candidate\u202fC, while urging the panel to probe B\u2019s and D\u2019s interpersonal dynamics further."}
